  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender Partnerships, Research and Advocacy Initiative (Global and Asia-Pacific) 2019 - 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Partnerships, Research and Advocacy initiative supports delivery of better aid programs through research and capacity building. A range of research activities have been supported under this initiative, including: the OECD&apos;s Development Assistance Committee&apos;s DAC Network on Gender Equality (GENDERNET). GENDERNET is an international forum where experts from development co-operation agencies meet to define common approaches in support of gender equality and women&#x2019;s rights. Currently active activities under this investment support the World Bank Group and its client countries and partners to gather global and country level data and evidence to make the case for childcare, develop quality approaches and build capacity, and provide project finance to incentivise countries to invest in childcare and scale implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
